# Catalog build (issue #6): the recordings are binaries, everything else is the record.
# facts.jsonl, ddo-ipa.json, prompts/ and out/ are all committed on purpose — out/ is the
# expensive artefact, and the other three are what makes it reproducible and checkable.
/catalog/audio/
/catalog/audio-manifest.json
/words.txt
/kaikki.org-dictionary-Danish.jsonl
/freq-30k-ex.txt
/freq-30k-in.txt
/ddo-fullforms_*.csv

# Azure corpus generation (issue #16): a raw per-call log and a rebuildable translation cache —
# transient operational output, not curated content. The cost/character totals that matter are
# reported in commit messages instead.
/catalog/families/azure-usage.json
/catalog/families/translation-cache.json
